The English word 'drop' can function as both a noun and a verb, while Thai often requires different words to convey the same meaning depending on the context. In some situations, a term that works as a noun in English may be better translated as a verb in Thai. This glossary should be used as a general guideline and not as a strict rule. | Example: ราคาลง £36

